window.CAUSOS={"jardineiro":{"steps":[{"s":0,"who":"Narrator","txt":"Before I was a professor, I was an engineering student who got a job on campus as the gardener. One day I was raking up cut grass while a civil engineering class had its surveying lesson right there in the garden."},{"s":0,"who":"Narrator","txt":"Their challenge sat at the far end: two fenced walls met at an unknown angle. And from the stake where the theodolite had to stand, the corner was hidden behind a mango tree. The class was stuck."},{"s":1,"who":"Gardener","txt":"Why don't you shoot at least two points on each wall and extend the lines until they cross?"},{"s":2,"who":"Narrator","txt":"Two points make a line. Two lines give you the corner nobody can see. It is more or less what I still do with data: work out what is hidden from what can be measured."},{"s":3,"who":"The class","txt":"Who is that guy? The gardener knows surveying? Good grief. (I just kept raking and walked off.)"},{"s":4,"who":"Narrator","txt":"What they did not know: the gardener was the teaching assistant for GIS, remote sensing and hydrology, and a technician in three labs. In 2015 I came back to the classroom, on the other side of the desk."}]},"batman":{"steps":[{"s":0,"who":"Narrator","txt":"In college my nickname was Batman. No cape involved: I just rescued a lot of people as a teaching assistant."},{"s":1,"who":"Narrator","txt":"Someone got stuck on a subject, and up went the signal."},{"s":2,"who":"Narrator","txt":"I could see why the class struggled with the way the professor taught it, and I could teach it my way. I was the one who explained things."}]},"radio":{"steps":[{"s":0,"who":"Narrator","txt":"In my last year of high school we ran an online radio station. The programming was tutoring: we solved problem sets live, in chemistry, physics, math and geography."},{"s":1,"who":"Narrator","txt":"We covered philosophy too. The audience was my own class, each at home. An educational podcast, except nobody had told us those existed."}]},"banda":{"steps":[{"s":0,"who":"Narrator","txt":"In high school I had a band, grew my hair out and was sure I was Slash. I even tried a Guns N' Roses cover band; they were my favorite for years."},{"s":1,"who":"Narrator","txt":"What I actually looked like was Cauby Peixoto, a Brazilian crooner famous for his enormous hair. Think less hard rock, more Vegas lounge."},{"s":2,"who":"Narrator","txt":"I ended up cutting it and getting job training through PROMAM, a social program for young people. I worked while finishing school: painted houses and trucks, washed cars, ran errands as an office boy, worked at a bike shop and at a garage."}]},"uno":{"steps":[{"s":0,"who":"Narrator","txt":"I owned a very troubled 1992 Fiat Uno. I did the repairs myself, since the garage job had taught me a thing or two. One night, in the small hours, water got into the carburetor."},{"s":1,"who":"Narrator","txt":"The engineering solution: I poured fuel on it and dried the carburetor with fire. It started. I made it home."},{"s":2,"who":"Narrator","txt":"Another time the fuel pump died. I patched it with a plastic bag and epoxy putty and drove more than 200 km. I do not recommend it. The car also used to catch fire along the fuel line all by itself, no help from me."}]},"fatbob":{"steps":[{"s":0,"who":"Narrator","txt":"I rode a bike without training wheels at age 2. I also learned to read at 2. It was a productive year."},{"s":1,"who":"Narrator","txt":"Then I fell for BMX racing, then mountain biking, then dirt jumping."},{"s":2,"who":"Narrator","txt":"That eventually turned into motorcycles. My first was a sand-colored 2014 Harley-Davidson Fat Bob."}]},"eletrosom":{"steps":[{"s":0,"who":"Narrator","txt":"I sold appliances at Eletrosom, a retail chain. Sometimes the customer was a farmer from a tiny rural community. The logistics fix: ship the furniture and appliances through the bus station."},{"s":1,"who":"Narrator","txt":"The bus took it from there. All of it ran on trust."},{"s":2,"who":"Narrator","txt":"And in the end it paid off in a wheel of cheese. A jar of mango sweet. A chicken. Still the best loyalty program I know."}]},"sitio":{"steps":[{"s":0,"who":"Narrator","txt":"During the pandemic I set up a woodshop in the garage and a small farm. Vegetables, chickens, cattle."},{"s":1,"who":"Narrator","txt":"And automation, of course: water from the fish tanks irrigates the vegetables. I also built a hydraulic ram, the pump that lifts water with no electricity, using only the water's own hammer."},{"s":2,"who":"Narrator","txt":"Hydraulics was the first course I ever taught. At home it turned into garden beds. Almost a MacGyver."}]}};
